ns.guideText = {
  ["forever.hunter"] = "A bow or a gun, a pet, and a lot of distance. Auto Shot, Raptor Strike and Track Beasts are yours from the start, Serpent Sting and Aspect of the Monkey come at 4, Hunter's Mark and Arcane Shot at 6. At 10 a class quest gives you a pet, and Aspect of the Hawk comes with it. Every line below says where to stand, what to shoot and when to send the pet.",
  ["forever.hunter-beast-mastery.dry"] = "A dead pet leaves you alone with the monster, so keep it mended.",
  ["forever.hunter-beast-mastery.intro"] = "Beast Mastery makes the pet the other half of your damage. Deadly Aspects speeds your shots, Summon Hawk lets two hawks fight beside your pet from 25, and Bestial Wrath makes the pet hit much harder at 40. It is the easiest Hunter to level.",
  ["forever.hunter-beast-mastery.line"] = "Your pet and two hawks do much of the work. The easiest Hunter to level, and the pet carries the pulls.",
  ["forever.hunter-beast-mastery.note"] = "(31 points in Beast Mastery, then 20 in Marksmanship for critical hits and Mortal Shots.)",
  ["forever.hunter-beast-mastery.p1"] = "With Aspect of the Hawk on, Auto Shot sometimes speeds up your shooting by 30% for 12 seconds. The full orders start here.",
  ["forever.hunter-beast-mastery.p10"] = "Your pet stuns the monster for 3 seconds on its next hit, and that hit crits far more often. It is the way to Bestial Wrath.",
  ["forever.hunter-beast-mastery.p11"] = "Ferocity is full, which opens Frenzy.",
  ["forever.hunter-beast-mastery.p12"] = "Doubles your pet's Focus regeneration and lets half your mana regeneration go on while you cast. Kargoz takes it here, Vareion at 38.",
  ["forever.hunter-beast-mastery.p13"] = "After a critical hit your pet sometimes attacks 30% faster for 8 seconds. Kargoz stops at four points, Vareion takes five.",
  ["forever.hunter-beast-mastery.p14"] = "You and your pet regain 1% of your health every 5 seconds while the pet is out. Kargoz takes one point, Vareion none.",
  ["forever.hunter-beast-mastery.p15"] = "Your pet deals 50% more damage for 18 seconds. It is the end of the tree, and every point before it was spent to reach it.",
  ["forever.hunter-beast-mastery.p16"] = "1% more critical strike chance on all your attacks. The Marksmanship points start here in both full orders.",
  ["forever.hunter-beast-mastery.p17"] = "6 yards more range on your ranged weapons. More range is more time before the monster reaches you.",
  ["forever.hunter-beast-mastery.p18"] = "Your attack power rises by your Intellect, so gear with Intellect pays twice, in mana and in damage.",
  ["forever.hunter-beast-mastery.p19"] = "Rapid Fire comes back 2 minutes sooner, and a kill under your Serpent Sting makes your next shot hit 20% harder.",
  ["forever.hunter-beast-mastery.p2"] = "2% more damage for you and your pet while the pet is out. It is the one talent on this row that adds damage.",
  ["forever.hunter-beast-mastery.p20"] = "Critical hits with ranged abilities deal 30% more. It needs Careful Aim, so it comes last.",
  ["forever.hunter-beast-mastery.p3"] = "Revive Pet casts 6 seconds faster and costs 40% less mana. These two points help reach the ten that row 2 asks for. Pathfinding cannot come before ten points.",
  ["forever.hunter-beast-mastery.p4"] = "15% more health and armour for your pet. This point is the tenth, which opens row 2, and a tougher pet holds a pull longer.",
  ["forever.hunter-beast-mastery.p5"] = "Your pet moves 30% faster. Intimidation needs it, and Bestial Wrath needs Intimidation.",
  ["forever.hunter-beast-mastery.p6"] = "Your pets and hawks deal up to 20% more damage, and the hawks of Summon Hawk count. Kargoz and Vareion both take all five.",
  ["forever.hunter-beast-mastery.p7"] = "A hawk dives at the monster, hits at once and keeps attacking for 18 seconds. Two hawks can be out together. Kargoz calls it a huge power spike.",
  ["forever.hunter-beast-mastery.p8"] = "Your pets and hawks deal the full 20% more damage once this point is in.",
  ["forever.hunter-beast-mastery.p9"] = "Your pet and hawks crit up to 16% more often. Frenzy needs all five points, so these come first.",
  ["forever.hunter-beast-mastery.s1"] = "Before your first talent point and before your pet. The same kit in every build. Pull from as far as you can reach and back away from what gets close.",
