  ["forever.hunter-marksmanship.split"] = "the last twenty points. This order is Vareion's, with nine in Beast Mastery. Icy Veins' picture at level 58 has 17 in Beast Mastery with Summon Hawk among them, and a variant of Vareion's swaps the last two points for Lone Wolf, which Warcraft Tavern would not take while levelling.",
  ["forever.hunter-survival.dry"] = "Do not walk in before Auto Shot has fired.",
  ["forever.hunter-survival.intro"] = "Survival is the Hunter who walks in. Savage Strikes and Predator's Edge make the melee strikes hit harder, Expose Prey lets your Hunter's Mark trigger Mongoose Bite, and Strider Kick gets you out again. It is the slowest Hunter to level and comes online between 30 and 40.",
  ["forever.hunter-survival.line"] = "Shoot, step in for Raptor Strike and Mongoose Bite, then back out. The slowest to level, and it comes online between 30 and 40.",
  ["forever.hunter-survival.note"] = "(35 points in Survival, 11 in Marksmanship and 5 in Beast Mastery.)",
  ["forever.hunter-survival.p1"] = "5% more damage to the kind of creature you are tracking. Track what you are fighting, or these points do nothing.",
  ["forever.hunter-survival.p10"] = "The last point of the 30% more critical damage on your melee abilities.",
  ["forever.hunter-survival.p11"] = "A kick for full weapon damage that makes you move 30% faster for 3 seconds. It is how you step out of melee.",
  ["forever.hunter-survival.p12"] = "The fifth point of Deflection. Feor leaves Deflection out of his end game, and here it is a point toward the 25 that Lightning Reflexes asks for.",
  ["forever.hunter-survival.p13"] = "15% more Agility, which is attack power and crit for a hunter.",
  ["forever.hunter-survival.p14"] = "Mongoose Bite also leaves a bleed for 40% of its damage over 21 seconds. It is the end of the tree.",
  ["forever.hunter-survival.p15"] = "With Aspect of the Hawk on, Auto Shot sometimes speeds up your shooting by 30% for 12 seconds. Vareion takes it right after the tree.",
  ["forever.hunter-survival.p16"] = "Your traps and melee strikes cost 60% less mana, and critical hits let half your mana regeneration go on while you cast.",
  ["forever.hunter-survival.p17"] = "1% more critical strike chance on all your attacks. The Marksmanship points start here.",
  ["forever.hunter-survival.p18"] = "Your attack power rises by your Intellect, so gear with Intellect pays twice, in mana and in damage.",
  ["forever.hunter-survival.p19"] = "Your Immolation and Explosive traps deal 30% more, and Freezing and Frost traps last 30% longer. Feor takes both points.",
  ["forever.hunter-survival.p2"] = "20% more critical strike chance on all your melee abilities, which is what Raptor Strike and Mongoose Bite need.",
  ["forever.hunter-survival.p20"] = "Serpent Sting deals up to 20% more. This last point is ours: Vareion's Lone Wolf does nothing while you keep a pet.",
  ["forever.hunter-survival.p3"] = "5% more parry chance. A parry is what lets Counterattack work.",
  ["forever.hunter-survival.p4"] = "3% more hit chance, and movement slows on you last 30% less. Both help a hunter who walks in and out.",
  ["forever.hunter-survival.p5"] = "Deterrence raises your dodge and parry by 25% for 10 seconds. It opens Counterattack.",
  ["forever.hunter-survival.p6"] = "A fourth point of Deflection, more parries.",
  ["forever.hunter-survival.p7"] = "A strike after a parry that cannot be blocked, dodged or parried and roots the monster for 5 seconds. Vareion calls it core.",
  ["forever.hunter-survival.p8"] = "Your melee abilities crit for 30% more and your off hand hits 50% harder,. Expose Prey is the next row.",
  ["forever.hunter-survival.p9"] = "Attacks on a monster with your Hunter's Mark have a 10% chance to let you use Mongoose Bite. Lacerating Strikes needs both points.",
  ["forever.hunter-survival.s1"] = "Before your first talent point and before your pet. The same kit in every build. Pull from as far as you can reach and back away from what gets close.",
  ["forever.hunter-survival.s1.between1.if"] = "before you leave town",
