  ["forever.mage-fire.split"] = "one guide only. Mobalytics has the only full Fire order, and the others describe how it plays. Warcraft Tavern builds around Improved Scorch, which Mobalytics skips, and Conquest Capped treats Fire as a build for the first 20 levels. The order here is Mobalytics'.",
  ["forever.mage-frost.dry"] = "Frost Nova freezes a monster until something hurts it, so let that something be Ice Lance.",
  ["forever.mage-frost.intro"] = "Frost slows and freezes what reaches you, and hits a frozen monster hard with Ice Lance. Most guides level it, because a monster that cannot reach you cannot hurt you.",
  ["forever.mage-frost.line"] = "Frostbolt, Frost Nova and Ice Lance on a frozen monster. The safest way to level alone.",
  ["forever.mage-frost.note"] = "(39 points in Frost, then 12 in Arcane for mana.)",
  ["forever.mage-frost.p1"] = "Frostbolt is most of what you cast, and each rank shortens the cast, so more of them land before the monster reaches you.",
  ["forever.mage-frost.p10"] = "Resets your Frost cooldowns, Frost Nova above all. It is also the gate to Ice Barrier, so it is here for what comes after.",
  ["forever.mage-frost.p11"] = "Cone of Cold hits harder. It is what you cast on a monster at your feet when Frost Nova is not ready.",
  ["forever.mage-frost.p12"] = "Frostbolt, and the Ice Lance from Fingers of Frost, make your next Cone of Cold hit harder, and it stacks. Cone of Cold is where it pays.",
  ["forever.mage-frost.p13"] = "A shield that raises your Frost damage, and while it holds a hit does not slow your casts. Keep it up before every pull. It needs Cold Snap.",
  ["forever.mage-frost.p14"] = "The last rank, taken with the points left after Ice Barrier.",
  ["forever.mage-frost.p15"] = "Chills freeze more often, which feeds Ice Lance and Shatter.",
  ["forever.mage-frost.p16"] = "Frost spells cost less mana and cause less threat. Mana is the limit of the class, and this is the plainest way to cast more.",
  ["forever.mage-frost.p17"] = "Blizzard slows what it hits. Take it if you pull groups or run dungeons, and spend the points elsewhere if you do neither.",
  ["forever.mage-frost.p18"] = "The first Arcane points, for mana. Five points open Arcane's second row, and your Arcane casts sometimes lose less time when you are hit.",
  ["forever.mage-frost.p19"] = "Frostbolt now sometimes makes your next Arcane Missiles shorter and free. Cast the Missiles when it lights up.",
  ["forever.mage-frost.p2"] = "Fewer misses on every spell. A resisted Frostbolt is mana spent and a monster closer, so it is worth taking early.",
  ["forever.mage-frost.p20"] = "Your spells are resisted less. A small gain, taken because the points after it are for mana.",
  ["forever.mage-frost.p21"] = "Your damage spells sometimes make the next spell free. The best Arcane point for a build that wants to cast more.",
  ["forever.mage-frost.p3"] = "Your chills can freeze the target. A frozen monster is the one Ice Lance hits hardest, so this is where that hit starts.",
  ["forever.mage-frost.p4"] = "Your hardest single hit, instant, and far harder on a frozen monster. It sits in the third row, so it waits for ten points in Frost.",
  ["forever.mage-frost.p5"] = "Frost critical hits do more damage. Frostbolt is nearly every cast you make, so this lifts the whole build.",
  ["forever.mage-frost.p6"] = "Makes you immune for a few seconds. It is the answer to the pull that went wrong, and you cannot act while inside it.",
  ["forever.mage-frost.p7"] = "Your spells crit more often against a frozen target. That is the target Ice Lance is aimed at.",
  ["forever.mage-frost.p8"] = "The last rank of the critical damage bonus.",
  ["forever.mage-frost.p9"] = "Your chills can make the next 2 spells hit as if the target were frozen. It needs Ice Lance, and it gives you Ice Lances on monsters that never froze.",
  ["forever.mage-frost.s1"] = "Before your first talent point. The same kit in every build.",
  ["forever.mage-frost.s1.between1.if"] = "when your bags have none",
  ["forever.mage-frost.s1.between1.why"] = "drinking is how your mana comes back",
