  ["forever.mage-frost.s4.rarely4.if"] = "on a second monster that joins",
  ["forever.mage-frost.s4.rarely4.why"] = "a sheep does not attack until it is damaged",
  ["forever.mage-frost.split"] = "the first points and the tail. Mobalytics takes Improved Frostbolt first, Conquest Capped would take Precision first for monsters above your level, and Icy Veins opens in Arcane for Missile Barrage. After 40 Mobalytics goes to Arcane for mana, Conquest Capped to Fire. The Arcane tail is Mobalytics'.",
  ["forever.mage.advice.damage"] = "Frost is the build this page advises, because it keeps monsters off you. Arcane is the other road guides name, and Method says it out-damages Frost when you quest alone.",
  ["forever.mage.ov.bad"] = "Being hit. You have little health and a cast that is interrupted is a turn lost. Two monsters at once is the usual way a mage dies.",
  ["forever.mage.ov.good"] = "Damage at range, and keeping monsters away with slows, freezes and a sheep. You make your own food and water, and you can carry a group's.",
  ["forever.mage.ov.levelling"] = "Frostbolt from as far as you can reach, Frost Nova when it gets close, step back and cast again. Drink between pulls. Pull one monster at a time until you are sure.",
  ["forever.mage.ov.resource"] = "Mana, and it is the whole game. Every cast spends it, so you cast, wait and drink. The wand costs none, and you must stand still to use it.",
  ["forever.mage.ov.ten"] = "You get your first talent point. Pick a build and Primer shows your first picks. Frost is the safest way to level alone, and a respec costs gold.",
  ["forever.mage.ov.who"] = "You hurt things from a distance with a cast bar and a mana bar. The craft is what to cast and when to stand still, and a monster that reaches you has won a round.",
  ["forever.mage.role.damage"] = "Most guides level Frost. It slows and freezes what reaches you, and Ice Lance on a frozen monster hits hardest.",
  ["forever.rogue"] = "Energy is the whole class, and combo points are what you spend it on. Sinister Strike, Eviscerate and Stealth are yours from the start, Sprint, Slice and Dice and Sap come at 10, Shank at 24. Every line below is a strike, a finisher or a way out.",
  ["forever.rogue-assassination.dry"] = "A monster immune to poison takes Mutilate at its plain damage.",
  ["forever.rogue-assassination.intro"] = "Assassination lives on poisons and Mutilate, which comes at 42. Until then it plays like any rogue with a dagger. Guides call it a slow way to level, and guides want a dagger in each hand.",
  ["forever.rogue-assassination.line"] = "Poisons, Shank and Mutilate with daggers. Slow until 42, then the hardest single hits.",
  ["forever.rogue-assassination.note"] = "(34 points in Assassination, then 12 in Combat and 5 in Subtlety.)",
  ["forever.rogue-assassination.p1"] = "After a kill, your next strike is more likely to crit for a short time. Go straight to the next monster and it pays.",
  ["forever.rogue-assassination.p10"] = "Shank also raises your poison damage and how often poisons land for a few seconds. Mutilate needs it, so it comes before Mutilate.",
  ["forever.rogue-assassination.p11"] = "Finishers sometimes give back 25 Energy, more often the more points they spend. More Energy means more strikes.",
  ["forever.rogue-assassination.p12"] = "A critical hit from a strike sometimes adds another combo point, so finishers come sooner.",
  ["forever.rogue-assassination.p13"] = "Finishers sometimes give back 25 Energy, more often the more points they spend. More Energy means more strikes.",
  ["forever.rogue-assassination.p14"] = "Poisons land more often and sometimes spend no charge, so you coat your weapons less.",
  ["forever.rogue-assassination.p15"] = "Hits with both weapons, harder on a poisoned monster, and gives 2 combo points. It replaces Sinister Strike and needs a dagger.",
  ["forever.rogue-assassination.p16"] = "Eviscerate hits harder. It ends most fights, so this pays on every kill.",
  ["forever.rogue-assassination.p17"] = "You parry more often, and a parry is what lights Riposte. Some hits simply stop landing.",
  ["forever.rogue-assassination.p18"] = "Fewer misses. A strike that misses is Energy spent for nothing, and a rogue has little to spare.",
  ["forever.rogue-assassination.p19"] = "After a parry, Riposte hits harder than a strike for little Energy and disarms the monster. Press it whenever it lights.",
  ["forever.rogue-assassination.p2"] = "Sinister Strike costs less Energy, and you press it until Mutilate. A cheap strike lets you press more of them.",
  ["forever.rogue-assassination.p20"] = "Fewer misses. A strike that misses is Energy spent for nothing, and a rogue has little to spare.",
  ["forever.rogue-assassination.p21"] = "Backstab, Garrote, Ambush and Mutilate hit harder. Mutilate is your main strike, so most of it lands there.",
  ["forever.rogue-assassination.p22"] = "Your poisons do more damage. A modest gain, taken last because the points have nowhere better to go.",
  ["forever.rogue-assassination.p3"] = "More critical strikes with every attack and poison. Critical hits are where a rogue's damage comes from.",
  ["forever.rogue-assassination.p4"] = "Slice and Dice lasts longer, so you refresh it less and strike more.",
  ["forever.rogue-assassination.p5"] = "More critical strikes with every attack and poison. Critical hits are where a rogue's damage comes from.",
  ["forever.rogue-assassination.p6"] = "A bigger Energy bar. You can spend more before you have to wait.",
  ["forever.rogue-assassination.p7"] = "Your finishers sometimes add a combo point to the monster, so the next finisher comes sooner.",
  ["forever.rogue-assassination.p8"] = "Your next strike or Eviscerate is a certain critical hit. Keep it for the hit that matters, and press it again when it is ready.",
  ["forever.rogue-assassination.p9"] = "Poisons land more often and sometimes spend no charge, so you coat your weapons less.",
  ["forever.rogue-assassination.s1"] = "Before your first talent point. The same kit in every build.",
  ["forever.rogue-assassination.s1.between1.if"] = "after a fight, before the next pull",
  ["forever.rogue-assassination.s1.between1.text"] = "Bandage or eat",
  ["forever.rogue-assassination.s1.between1.why"] = "Energy comes back by itself, health does not",
  ["forever.rogue-assassination.s1.loop1.if"] = "when a second monster joins",
  ["forever.rogue-assassination.s1.loop1.why"] = "it holds one still while you kill the other",
  ["forever.rogue-assassination.s1.loop2.if"] = "when a monster hits hard",
  ["forever.rogue-assassination.s1.loop2.why"] = "you dodge more while it lasts",
  ["forever.rogue-assassination.s1.loop3.if"] = "when the monster is about to die",
  ["forever.rogue-assassination.s1.loop3.why"] = "left-over points are wasted when it dies",
  ["forever.rogue-assassination.s1.loop4.why"] = "it hits and builds the points Eviscerate spends",
  ["forever.rogue-assassination.s1.low1.if"] = "when your Energy is empty",
  ["forever.rogue-assassination.s1.low1.why"] = "swings still land while Energy comes back",
  ["forever.rogue-assassination.s1.opening1.if"] = "before the pull, if you can reach it unseen",
  ["forever.rogue-assassination.s1.opening1.why"] = "you strike first and it has not seen you",
  ["forever.rogue-assassination.s1.opening2.if"] = "from behind with a dagger",
  ["forever.rogue-assassination.s1.opening2.why"] = "it hits hard and gives you a combo point",
  ["forever.rogue-assassination.s2"] = "Slice and Dice, Sprint and Sap arrive at 10, Ambush and Poised at 18. A dagger in the main hand now, for Backstab and Ambush.",
  ["forever.rogue-assassination.s2.between1.if"] = "after a fight, before the next pull",
  ["forever.rogue-assassination.s2.between1.text"] = "Bandage or eat",
  ["forever.rogue-assassination.s2.between1.why"] = "Energy comes back by itself, health does not",
  ["forever.rogue-assassination.s2.loop1.if"] = "when a monster starts a spell",
  ["forever.rogue-assassination.s2.loop1.why"] = "it stops the cast",
  ["forever.rogue-assassination.s2.loop2.if"] = "when it has run out",
  ["forever.rogue-assassination.s2.loop2.why"] = "your swings come faster for the whole fight",
  ["forever.rogue-assassination.s2.loop3.if"] = "at 4 or 5 combo points",
  ["forever.rogue-assassination.s2.loop3.why"] = "it spends the points on one big hit",
  ["forever.rogue-assassination.s2.loop4.if"] = "when you are behind with a dagger",
  ["forever.rogue-assassination.s2.loop4.why"] = "it hits hard and gives you a combo point",
  ["forever.rogue-assassination.s2.loop5.why"] = "it builds the points when Backstab cannot",
  ["forever.rogue-assassination.s2.low1.if"] = "when your Energy is empty",
  ["forever.rogue-assassination.s2.low1.why"] = "swings still land while Energy comes back",
  ["forever.rogue-assassination.s2.opening1.if"] = "before the pull, out of combat",
  ["forever.rogue-assassination.s2.opening1.text"] = "Open at full Energy",
  ["forever.rogue-assassination.s2.opening1.why"] = "Poised takes Energy off your first ability",
  ["forever.rogue-assassination.s2.opening2.if"] = "before the pull, if you can reach it unseen",
  ["forever.rogue-assassination.s2.opening2.why"] = "you strike first and it has not seen you",
  ["forever.rogue-assassination.s2.opening3.if"] = "with a dagger, or Garrote on a long fight",
  ["forever.rogue-assassination.s2.opening3.why"] = "it is the hardest hit you have for a first strike",
  ["forever.rogue-assassination.s2.rarely1.if"] = "when a second monster joins",
  ["forever.rogue-assassination.s2.rarely1.why"] = "it holds one still while you kill the other",
  ["forever.rogue-assassination.s2.rarely2.if"] = "when a monster hits hard",
  ["forever.rogue-assassination.s2.rarely2.why"] = "you dodge more while it lasts",
  ["forever.rogue-assassination.s2.rarely3.if"] = "on one of two humanoids, before the pull",
  ["forever.rogue-assassination.s2.rarely3.why"] = "it sleeps until something hurts it",
  ["forever.rogue-assassination.s2.rarely4.if"] = "on a monster that will last a long time",
  ["forever.rogue-assassination.s2.rarely4.why"] = "it lowers its armour so you hit harder",
  ["forever.rogue-assassination.s2.rarely5.if"] = "to close in or to leave",
  ["forever.rogue-assassination.s2.rarely5.why"] = "you move much faster for a moment",
  ["forever.rogue-assassination.s3"] = "Poisons at 20, Shank at 24, Cheap Shot at 26. Venom at 32 makes Shank also strengthen your poisons. Your damage is still plain until Mutilate.",
  ["forever.rogue-assassination.s3.between1.if"] = "when the coating is gone",
  ["forever.rogue-assassination.s3.between1.text"] = "Coat both weapons in poison",
  ["forever.rogue-assassination.s3.between1.why"] = "each hit may poison, and it costs no Energy",
  ["forever.rogue-assassination.s3.between2.if"] = "after a fight, before the next pull",
  ["forever.rogue-assassination.s3.between2.text"] = "Bandage or eat",
  ["forever.rogue-assassination.s3.between2.why"] = "Energy comes back by itself, health does not",
  ["forever.rogue-assassination.s3.big"] = "before the Eviscerate that matters most",
  ["forever.rogue-assassination.s3.loop1.if"] = "when it is ready and Energy is not full",
  ["forever.rogue-assassination.s3.loop1.why"] = "it gives back more Energy than it costs",
