  ["forever.rogue-assassination.s4.rarely6.if"] = "to get away from a monster you cannot beat",
  ["forever.rogue-assassination.s4.rarely6.why"] = "it wanders off blind while you leave",
  ["forever.rogue-assassination.split"] = "the whole order. Mobalytics' Djexde gives the only full order and says to level Combat instead. Icy Veins names the same key talents (Remorseless Attacks, Ruthlessness, Relentless Strikes, Lethality, Cold Blood, Seal Fate, Venom) but its order sits in a slider that could not be read. Method, as read, prefers Assassination.",
  ["forever.rogue-combat.dry"] = "Riposte only lights after a parry, so face the monster and let it swing.",
  ["forever.rogue-combat.intro"] = "Combat swings two weapons and leans on Riposte, Shank and Blade Flurry. It is the build most guides level, because it is smooth and wastes little. Take a sword, axe or mace, and a dagger only if you must.",
  ["forever.rogue-combat.line"] = "Sinister Strike, Riposte after a parry, Blade Flurry for two. The smoothest way to level a rogue.",
  ["forever.rogue-combat.note"] = "(35 points in Combat, then 16 in Assassination for critical hits and poisons.)",
  ["forever.rogue-combat.p1"] = "Sinister Strike costs less Energy, and it is the strike you press most. More of them land before the monster is dead.",
  ["forever.rogue-combat.p10"] = "Fewer of your strikes are dodged or parried. Monsters in front of you do both often, so every point wastes less.",
  ["forever.rogue-combat.p11"] = "Sinister Strike and Eviscerate hit a little harder, and they are most of your damage.",
  ["forever.rogue-combat.p12"] = "Your swings come faster and each hit also strikes a second monster nearby. This is how a rogue takes two at once. Press it with Evasion.",
  ["forever.rogue-combat.p13"] = "Your off-hand hits harder. You swing two weapons all fight, so it pays on every swing.",
  ["forever.rogue-combat.p14"] = "Swords and axes sometimes swing again for free, daggers and fists add critical chance, maces ignore armour. Carry the weapon that fits it.",
  ["forever.rogue-combat.p15"] = "Shank gives back more Energy and comes round sooner. The more you press it, the less you wait.",
  ["forever.rogue-combat.p16"] = "A burst of Energy for a hard fight. Press it with Blade Flurry when your Energy is nearly empty.",
  ["forever.rogue-combat.p17"] = "More critical strikes with every attack and poison. Critical hits are where a rogue's damage comes from.",
  ["forever.rogue-combat.p18"] = "Your finishers sometimes add a combo point to the monster, so the next finisher comes sooner.",
  ["forever.rogue-combat.p19"] = "Slice and Dice lasts longer, so you refresh it less and strike more.",
  ["forever.rogue-combat.p2"] = "Eviscerate hits harder. It ends most fights, so this pays on every kill.",
  ["forever.rogue-combat.p20"] = "Critical hits from your strikes hurt more. It needs Malice at full, and Malice is worth having anyway.",
  ["forever.rogue-combat.p21"] = "Swords and axes sometimes swing again for free, daggers and fists add critical chance, maces ignore armour. Carry the weapon that fits it.",
  ["forever.rogue-combat.p22"] = "Sinister Strike and Eviscerate hit a little harder, and they are most of your damage.",
  ["forever.rogue-combat.p23"] = "Slice and Dice lasts longer, so you refresh it less and strike more.",
  ["forever.rogue-combat.p24"] = "Expose Armor costs less Energy and gives points back when cast at 5. Take it for the hard monsters.",
  ["forever.rogue-combat.p25"] = "Poisons land more often and sometimes spend no charge, so you coat your weapons less.",
  ["forever.rogue-combat.p3"] = "Fewer misses. A strike that misses is Energy spent for nothing, and a rogue has little to spare.",
  ["forever.rogue-combat.p4"] = "You parry more often, and a parry is what lights Riposte. Some hits simply stop landing.",
  ["forever.rogue-combat.p5"] = "After a parry, Riposte hits harder than Sinister Strike for little Energy and disarms the monster. Press it whenever it lights.",
  ["forever.rogue-combat.p6"] = "Fewer misses. A strike that misses is Energy spent for nothing, and a rogue has little to spare.",
  ["forever.rogue-combat.p7"] = "Sprint and Evasion come back sooner. A rogue's way out is its cooldowns, so shorter ones mean more fights you can leave.",
  ["forever.rogue-combat.p8"] = "Sprint breaks slows and roots as you press it. A monster that slows you can no longer hold you in the fight.",
  ["forever.rogue-combat.p9"] = "Eviscerate costs less Energy, so you finish sooner and start the next strike sooner.",
  ["forever.rogue-combat.s1"] = "Before your first talent point. The same kit in every build.",
  ["forever.rogue-combat.s1.between1.if"] = "after a fight, before the next pull",
  ["forever.rogue-combat.s1.between1.text"] = "Bandage or eat",
