  ["forever.rogue-combat.split"] = "the first points and the tail. DonTheCrown puts Precision at 2 first and reaches Riposte at 20 and Blade Flurry at 30, Djexde takes Remorseless Attacks first and reaches them at 22 and 32. This page follows DonTheCrown. Method would move points from Lightning Reflexes and Endurance into Puncturing Wounds for a dagger.",
  ["forever.rogue-subtlety.dry"] = "Backstab does nothing from the front, so walk round or use Hemorrhage.",
  ["forever.rogue-subtlety.intro"] = "Subtlety opens with Ambush and lives on Hemorrhage from 32. It is the sturdiest of the three at the start and the weakest on damage. The long way down the tree is the price.",
  ["forever.rogue-subtlety.line"] = "An Ambush opener, Ghostly Strike, Hemorrhage, then Death Mark at 42. Sturdy, and slower to kill.",
  ["forever.rogue-subtlety.note"] = "(31 points in Subtlety, then 14 in Combat and 6 in Assassination.)",
  ["forever.rogue-subtlety.p1"] = "After a kill, your next opener or strike is more likely to crit for a short time. It keeps you hitting hard between monsters.",
  ["forever.rogue-subtlety.p10"] = "Ambush, Garrote and Cheap Shot each add a combo point more. The opener becomes the first finisher.",
  ["forever.rogue-subtlety.p11"] = "Vanish and Blind come back much sooner. Your way out is ready for the next fight.",
  ["forever.rogue-subtlety.p12"] = "The build's main strike. It builds combo points with any weapon, from the front or behind, and makes your Rupture and Garrote hit harder.",
  ["forever.rogue-subtlety.p13"] = "Resets your cooldowns when a fight goes wrong, Evasion and Vanish with them. You hope not to press it, and Death Mark needs it.",
  ["forever.rogue-subtlety.p14"] = "A little less chance to be hit by spells and ranged attacks, and you spot hidden things sooner. Small, and it keeps the way down open.",
  ["forever.rogue-subtlety.p15"] = "You move faster in Stealth and Stealth is ready again sooner. Sneaking past monsters is how you skip fights.",
  ["forever.rogue-subtlety.p16"] = "Shank adds combo points to the monster every time. Press it on cooldown and your finishers come much sooner.",
  ["forever.rogue-subtlety.p17"] = "A finisher that stores your damage for a few seconds and then deals it. Use it on a long fight, with Garrote and Rupture bleeding.",
  ["forever.rogue-subtlety.p18"] = "Sinister Strike and Hemorrhage cost less Energy. Hemorrhage is your main strike, so this is the Energy you save most.",
  ["forever.rogue-subtlety.p19"] = "Eviscerate and Death Mark hit harder. Both end fights, so this pays on every kill.",
  ["forever.rogue-subtlety.p2"] = "You sometimes gain a combo point after a dodge. A small gain, taken because it opens the way down the tree.",
  ["forever.rogue-subtlety.p20"] = "You parry more often, and a parry is what lights Riposte. Some hits simply stop landing.",
  ["forever.rogue-subtlety.p21"] = "Fewer misses. A strike that misses is Energy spent for nothing, and a rogue has little to spare.",
  ["forever.rogue-subtlety.p22"] = "After a parry, Riposte hits harder than a strike for little Energy and disarms the monster. Press it whenever it lights.",
  ["forever.rogue-subtlety.p23"] = "Fewer misses. A strike that misses is Energy spent for nothing, and a rogue has little to spare.",
  ["forever.rogue-subtlety.p24"] = "Poised takes more Energy off your first ability after you rest. A small gain for the opener.",
  ["forever.rogue-subtlety.p25"] = "More critical strikes with every attack and poison. Critical hits are where a rogue's damage comes from.",
  ["forever.rogue-subtlety.p26"] = "Slice and Dice lasts longer, so you refresh it less and strike more.",
  ["forever.rogue-subtlety.p3"] = "Backstab, Garrote and Ambush hit harder. They are your openers, so every point counts.",
  ["forever.rogue-subtlety.p4"] = "Cheap Shot and Garrote cost less Energy, and Garrote no longer needs you behind the monster.",
  ["forever.rogue-subtlety.p5"] = "Backstab, Garrote and Ambush hit harder. They are your openers, so every point counts.",
  ["forever.rogue-subtlety.p6"] = "Your attacks ignore some armour and Rupture hits harder. It also leads to Hemorrhage.",
  ["forever.rogue-subtlety.p7"] = "Starts a fight with 2 combo points before the first strike. Press it just before Ambush or Garrote.",
  ["forever.rogue-subtlety.p8"] = "Ambush, Garrote and Cheap Shot each add a combo point more. The opener becomes the first finisher.",
  ["forever.rogue-subtlety.p9"] = "A strike that raises your dodge for a few seconds and lets Garrote or Ambush go without Stealth. Press it on cooldown.",
  ["forever.rogue-subtlety.s1"] = "Before your first talent point. The same kit in every build.",
  ["forever.rogue-subtlety.s1.between1.if"] = "after a fight, before the next pull",
  ["forever.rogue-subtlety.s1.between1.text"] = "Bandage or eat",
  ["forever.rogue-subtlety.s1.between1.why"] = "Energy comes back by itself, health does not",
  ["forever.rogue-subtlety.s1.loop1.if"] = "when a second monster joins",
  ["forever.rogue-subtlety.s1.loop1.why"] = "it holds one still while you kill the other",
  ["forever.rogue-subtlety.s1.loop2.if"] = "when a monster hits hard",
  ["forever.rogue-subtlety.s1.loop2.why"] = "you dodge more while it lasts",
  ["forever.rogue-subtlety.s1.loop3.if"] = "when the monster is about to die",
  ["forever.rogue-subtlety.s1.loop3.why"] = "left-over points are wasted when it dies",
  ["forever.rogue-subtlety.s1.loop4.why"] = "it hits and builds the points Eviscerate spends",
  ["forever.rogue-subtlety.s1.low1.if"] = "when your Energy is empty",
  ["forever.rogue-subtlety.s1.low1.why"] = "swings still land while Energy comes back",
  ["forever.rogue-subtlety.s1.opening1.if"] = "before the pull, if you can reach it unseen",
  ["forever.rogue-subtlety.s1.opening1.why"] = "you strike first and it has not seen you",
  ["forever.rogue-subtlety.s1.opening2.if"] = "from behind with a dagger",
  ["forever.rogue-subtlety.s1.opening2.why"] = "it hits hard and gives you a combo point",
  ["forever.rogue-subtlety.s2"] = "Slice and Dice, Sprint and Sap arrive at 10, Ambush at 18. Keep a dagger in the main hand: Ambush needs it and Hemorrhage hits harder with it.",
  ["forever.rogue-subtlety.s2.between1.if"] = "after a fight, before the next pull",
