  ["forever.rogue-subtlety.split"] = "the whole order. Mobalytics' Djexde gives a full order and advises Combat instead. Icy Veins agrees on the shape (Subtlety down to Hemorrhage, then Death Mark, then Combat, then Assassination) and its order sits in a slider that could not be read. Warcraft Tavern's Subtlety page and Kami Labs' simulation still use the talents removed before launch.",
  ["forever.rogue.advice.damage"] = "Combat is the build this page advises, because it is the smoothest to level, with Riposte at 20 and Blade Flurry at 30. The price: it wants a sword, axe or mace more than a dagger. Assassination wants daggers and is slow until Mutilate at 42. Subtlety is sturdy and slow to kill.",
  ["forever.rogue.ov.bad"] = "Being hit for long, and crowds. You wear leather and cannot heal, and you hurt one monster at a time. Bandages are your healing.",
  ["forever.rogue.ov.good"] = "Damage on one monster at a time, stuns and a sap to hold a fight still, and ways out: Vanish, Sprint, Evasion. You also skip fights by sneaking past what you do not want.",
  ["forever.rogue.ov.levelling"] = "Strike to build points, finish with Eviscerate or Slice and Dice, bandage between pulls. Learn First Aid early, it heals faster than eating. Sneak past what you can.",
  ["forever.rogue.ov.resource"] = "Energy, which fills back by itself, and combo points, which stay on the monster you built them on. Spend Energy on strikes, spend points on a finisher, and do not sit at full Energy.",
  ["forever.rogue.ov.ten"] = "You get your first talent point and pick a spec. Combat is the one most guides level. Assassination and Subtlety are the other two, and a respec costs gold.",
  ["forever.rogue.ov.who"] = "You open on a monster before it knows you are there, build combo points with strikes and spend them on a finisher. The craft is picking the fight, and knowing when to leave it.",
  ["forever.rogue.role.damage"] = "Most guides level Combat. Riposte hits hard from 20 and Blade Flurry takes two monsters at once from 30.",
  ["forever.shaman"] = "Totems, shocks and a weapon you imbue. Lightning Bolt and Healing Wave are yours from the start, Earth Shock comes at 4 and Lightning Shield at 8. At 10 a Fire totem and Flame Shock join, and Ghost Wolf follows at 20. Every line below says what to drop, what to press and when to stop and drink.",
  ["forever.shaman-elemental.dry"] = "Your mana is the slowest part of the fight, so finish a nearly dead monster with the weapon.",
  ["forever.shaman-elemental.intro"] = "Elemental opens with a shock and a bolt from a distance, and Lightning Overload and Lightning Mastery make the bolts hit twice and hit fast. It is slower to level than Enhancement because you stop to drink more often.",
  ["forever.shaman-elemental.line"] = "Lightning Bolt, Chain Lightning and Flame Shock from range. Strong in a group, slow alone, and hungry for mana.",
  ["forever.shaman-elemental.note"] = "(31 points in Elemental, 11 in Restoration for mana, 9 in Enhancement.)",
  ["forever.shaman-elemental.p1"] = "Shocks, Lightning Bolt and Chain Lightning cost 2% less a point. Mana is what stops a caster, so it comes first.",
  ["forever.shaman-elemental.p10"] = "Spells hit 5% more often, which a caster wants too. These points open Mindfulness and Water Shield.",
  ["forever.shaman-elemental.p11"] = "Some of your mana regeneration keeps going while you cast. You drink less, and the fight does not stop for it.",
  ["forever.shaman-elemental.p12"] = "Totems cost less mana. The points are on the way to Water Shield, which asks for ten in the tree.",
  ["forever.shaman-elemental.p13"] = "Globes of water give back mana when you are hit or land a critical strike. You give up Lightning Shield for it, since only one shield holds.",
  ["forever.shaman-elemental.p14"] = "Lightning Bolt and Chain Lightning get 5% more critical strike chance.",
  ["forever.shaman-elemental.p15"] = "Earthbind Totem roots nearby monsters for 5 seconds when you drop it. A pack stops and you keep casting.",
  ["forever.shaman-elemental.p16"] = "Critical hits from your fire, frost and nature spells do far more damage. It needs Lightning Overload.",
  ["forever.shaman-elemental.p17"] = "Your burst: for 15 seconds Chain Lightning has no cooldown and Lightning Bolt casts faster. Press it on a hard pull.",
  ["forever.shaman-elemental.p18"] = "Intellect: more mana, and more spell critical chance. Nothing left in the Elemental tree helps you more.",
  ["forever.shaman-elemental.p19"] = "More critical strikes on every spell and attack. It is the best that is left.",
  ["forever.shaman-elemental.p2"] = "Lightning Bolt and Chain Lightning cast faster. Lightning Overload needs it, and a faster cast is less time under a monster's claws.",
  ["forever.shaman-elemental.p3"] = "More damage on Lightning Bolt, Chain Lightning and Earth Shock, the spells you cast most.",
  ["forever.shaman-elemental.p4"] = "A damage spell can make your next one free. Spend the free cast on the dearest spell you have.",
  ["forever.shaman-elemental.p5"] = "Concussion at full strength: more damage on Lightning Bolt, Chain Lightning and Earth Shock.",
  ["forever.shaman-elemental.p6"] = "Your fire totems and Flame Shock hit harder, and Flame Shock lasts longer.",
  ["forever.shaman-elemental.p7"] = "Being hit while you cast has a good chance of not slowing Lightning Bolt and Chain Lightning. Fewer ruined casts.",
  ["forever.shaman-elemental.p8"] = "Flame Shock lasts longer and Searing Totem hurts more, so more of the work is done while you rest.",
  ["forever.shaman-elemental.p9"] = "Lightning Bolt and Chain Lightning can cast a second time for free, at half damage. Elemental Fury needs it.",
  ["forever.shaman-elemental.s1"] = "Before your first talent point. The same kit in every build.",
  ["forever.shaman-elemental.s1.between1.if"] = "after a fight, if you are hurt",
  ["forever.shaman-elemental.s1.between1.why"] = "it heals a lot for its mana",
  ["forever.shaman-elemental.s1.between2.if"] = "after a fight, before the next pull",
  ["forever.shaman-elemental.s1.between2.text"] = "Sit and drink",
  ["forever.shaman-elemental.s1.between2.why"] = "mana from drinking is cheap, and a pull on empty is not",
  ["forever.shaman-elemental.s1.loop1.if"] = "whenever it is ready",
  ["forever.shaman-elemental.s1.loop1.why"] = "it hits hard and stops a cast",
  ["forever.shaman-elemental.s1.loop2.if"] = "if the monster is still far",
  ["forever.shaman-elemental.s1.loop2.why"] = "a bolt lands before the monster does",
  ["forever.shaman-elemental.s1.loop3.why"] = "a swing costs no mana",
  ["forever.shaman-elemental.s1.low1.if"] = "when your mana is nearly gone",
  ["forever.shaman-elemental.s1.low1.why"] = "a swing costs no mana, and mana returns while you swing",
  ["forever.shaman-elemental.s1.opening1.if"] = "if it has worn off",
  ["forever.shaman-elemental.s1.opening1.why"] = "it adds attack power to every swing",
  ["forever.shaman-elemental.s1.opening2.if"] = "before the first pull",
  ["forever.shaman-elemental.s1.opening2.why"] = "its orbs hurt whatever hits you",
  ["forever.shaman-elemental.s1.opening3.if"] = "from as far away as it reaches",
  ["forever.shaman-elemental.s1.opening3.why"] = "the pull costs little and the monster walks to you",
  ["forever.shaman-elemental.s2"] = "Flame Shock and Searing Totem come at 10, Fire Nova at 12. Open with a shock, let the totem work, and finish a nearly dead monster with the weapon so your mana can start to return.",
  ["forever.shaman-elemental.s2.between1.if"] = "after a fight, if you are hurt",
