  ["forever.warrior-fury.split"] = "the points between Enrage and Gore Drinker and the last 20. Icy Veins takes Unbridled Wrath at 15 and Lingering Rage later, Kargoz does the reverse and skips Unbridled Wrath. Warcraft Tavern leaves Lingering Rage as an option. This page follows Kargoz, whose order is the newest.",
  ["forever.warrior-protection.dry"] = "A monster still on you when the fight is over means the job is working.",
  ["forever.warrior-protection.intro"] = "Protection holds monsters on you and stays up. It needs a shield, and Revenge from level 14 is what makes it kill. Before 14 use a two-hander.",
  ["forever.warrior-protection.line"] = "A shield, Revenge and Shield Slam. Holds monsters for a group, and the guides' pick for levelling alone.",
  ["forever.warrior-protection.note"] = "(31 points in Protection for Shield Slam, then 15 in Fury and 5 in Protection.)",
  ["forever.warrior-protection.p1"] = "More block, and each block gives you 5 rage. Shield Block pays for itself in two blocks.",
  ["forever.warrior-protection.p10"] = "More threat in Defensive Stance while you hold a shield, so monsters stay on you.",
  ["forever.warrior-protection.p11"] = "Every offensive ability costs less rage, so you can press more of them.",
  ["forever.warrior-protection.p12"] = "A stun, and Shield Slam needs it.",
  ["forever.warrior-protection.p13"] = "More threat in Defensive Stance while you hold a shield, so monsters stay on you.",
  ["forever.warrior-protection.p14"] = "More damage while you hold a shield, so the build kills faster.",
  ["forever.warrior-protection.p15"] = "A shield hit with very high threat and your best attack from level 40. It needs Concussion Blow and 30 points in Protection.",
  ["forever.warrior-protection.p16"] = "Melee critical hits come more often, and a critical hit gives you extra rage.",
  ["forever.warrior-protection.p17"] = "Your rage decays later once the fight is over, so a chain of pulls keeps its rage.",
  ["forever.warrior-protection.p18"] = "A hit may give you 1 more rage. It is small, but it is rage on every swing you make.",
  ["forever.warrior-protection.p19"] = "Bloodrage gives more rage for the same health.",
  ["forever.warrior-protection.p2"] = "Revenge hits much harder, and it is your main attack after a block, a dodge or a parry.",
  ["forever.warrior-protection.p20"] = "More Defense skill, so you are harder to hit and to crit. Spare points are well spent here.",
  ["forever.warrior-protection.p3"] = "Thunder Clap costs less rage, so you can keep a pack slowed.",
  ["forever.warrior-protection.p4"] = "A dodge or a parry with a shield can give you 5 rage. It needs Shield Specialization at full rank.",
  ["forever.warrior-protection.p5"] = "Thunder Clap costs less rage, so you can keep a pack slowed.",
  ["forever.warrior-protection.p6"] = "An emergency button: more health for a while, lost again after. Press it before you drop, not after.",
  ["forever.warrior-protection.p7"] = "More threat in Defensive Stance while you hold a shield, so monsters stay on you.",
  ["forever.warrior-protection.p8"] = "Charge works in Defensive Stance, so you open a fight without changing stance.",
  ["forever.warrior-protection.p9"] = "Sunder Armor costs less rage, and a tank wants it stacked on a long fight.",
  ["forever.warrior-protection.s1"] = "Before your first talent point. The same kit in every build.",
